[I] The WebSocket library in C

[T] Wslay is a WebSocket library written in C implementing protocol version
[T] 13 from RFC 6455. It offers an event-based API suited for non-blocking
[T] reactor style programs and a low-level frame-based API, handles text and
[T] binary messages and automatic ping replies, but performs no I/O or HTTP
[T] handshake on its own.

[U] https://tatsuhiro-t.github.io/wslay/

[A] Wslay Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

